  "body": "The fixed-reader P112 two-total support screen stopped at 43 source ports. At 44 ports, deletion geometry permits five retained rank losses, but **two correction columns cannot realize them**: the required cancellations contain a rank-three minor. This research note extends the no-saving range through **47 ports**.\n\n**Status: scoped negative result / research note; no new \u03ba or supplier.** The full-rank on-column case has COPY rank sum **at least 66**; combined with PR1197's complementary reductions, the general fixed-coordinate-reader two-total floor remains **64** through 47. No attainment of the 66 bill is claimed.\n\nAdds only `research/p112-joint-loss-boundary-seed49/`:\n\n- A written argument for arbitrary complex correction columns and ordinary transpose, backed by complete binary support/kernel inventories through 47.\n- All **672** minimal critical cancellation classes, all 56 coordinate-triple minors, the complete cross-reader obligations, and exact added-term pricing.\n- A full-rank overlapping two-total fixture attaining retained loss four (complete COPY bill **75**, sources outside `col(X)`), and a three-total negative control attaining loss five (bill 81). Both complete identities are checked on all 12,544 ordered port pairs; independent packed/unpacked rank implementations agree.\n- Source-drift, corrupted-receipt and hypothesis controls. `RESULT.json` is compared in full; the checker imports no predecessor verifier.\n\nBase: `0fdd7d82de03e43c9e5a1000dfbcd380d1b687d2`. Track: structural decoder research; fresh OS assignment seed **49**; priority revision 4. Exact source SHA256/Git blobs, task selection, stopping rule and predecessor heads are in `SOURCES.json`/`TASK.json`.\n\nValidation:\n\n```sh\npython3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/p112-joint-loss-boundary-seed49\n```\n\nPasses normally and under `-O`, ending `PASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE research/p112-joint-loss-boundary-seed49 outcome=completed`. A separate isolated export containing only this package and the pinned geometry also passes the direct `-I` checker. Metadata/pins and `git diff --check` pass. Hosted CI is separate; no selected-construction cold replay is needed for this isolated research package.\n\nScope: a separate-total COPY **rank-sum** obstruction, with other helper/access/frame/restoration/hosting/recursive charges optimistically zero. This does not compare power sums, price a complete supplier, or formalize multiplication. Source unions **48 or larger**, changed readers and masked identities are unexamined. The next useful step is the new minimal loss profiles at 48, tested for two-column realizability before treating deletion witnesses as feasible corrections.\n\nCredit: Josie Elliston's **PR1787** supplies generalized weights and the original support exclusion; Philipp/mightyOil's **PR1827** sharpens joint loss through 43 and **PR1197** supplies complementary reductions. Their predecessor attribution is retained in the README/proof. Pending **PR2338** restricts factors to the column space of a minimal-rank realisation, whereas this argument allows arbitrary source columns; its current head was rechecked and is not a dependency.\n\nCanonical main was refreshed unchanged. The final overlap snapshot covers **586 open PRs** and **1,114 discussion/comment/reply records**, complete pagination, no warnings (2026-10-15 07:04 UTC); the scoped terms matched only this package and its own claim. This is not a novelty guarantee. Coordination: [discussion 2369](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/2369).\n\nPrepared by **Sricharan Vagvala (@theon199)** with substantial **OpenAI Codex** assistance for mathematics, implementation, verification and writing. Parent-only execution; author-checked, no independent human review. Apache-2.0.\n",
